apt 2.7.14 CMake: include(CheckSymbolExists) for check_symbol_exists()

The top-level CMakeLists.txt calls check_symbol_exists(statfs ...) /
check_symbol_exists(statvfs ...) / CHECK_STRUCT_HAS_MEMBER without
including the CheckSymbolExists module.  On a Debian build the command
is pulled in transitively (or silently no-ops); on OHOS with a minimal
conan toolchain CMake fails with:

  CMake Error: Could not find CMAKE_ROOT
  ... Unknown CMake command "check_symbol_exists".

Fix by explicitly including CheckSymbolExists alongside the other
Check* modules already loaded.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 include(CheckIncludeFiles)
 include(CheckFunctionExists)
 include(CheckStructHasMember)
+include(CheckSymbolExists)
 include(GNUInstallDirs)
 include(TestBigEndian)
 find_package(Threads REQUIRED)
